WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.255
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.745 --> 00:00:07.120
CANDICE ERICKSON:
Today I'm going

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.400
to show you how to set
up a professional PHP

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.270
environment in the cloud using
Zend Server with the Google

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:13.860
Cloud Launcher.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.140
After starting the Cloud
Launcher home page,

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:19.610
click Infrastructure,
then click Zend Server.

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:23.110
Next, click Launch
on Compute Engine.

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:25.920
Select an existing project
or create a new one

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.960
for your Zend Server instance.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.720
For this example, I'll
pick an existing project,

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.650
then click Continue.

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:36.480
After the page loads, you can
configure your new instance.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.210
Give the instance a name
and deployment zone.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.180
You can also configure
additional details

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:42.780
that apply to your project.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:46.020
When you're finished, click the
Deploy button at the bottom.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.340
Once it is loaded, you'll
see all the details

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:51.300
you need to get started with
your Zend Server instance.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:54.490
Note the username and
password and click Launch.

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:57.140
That brings up the
Zend Server login page.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:00.190
Type your username and
password, and click Log In.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:02.410
That's all there is to it.

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:05.459
To get started with Zend
Server on Cloud Launcher, click

00:01:05.459 --> 00:01:07.030
on the link in the comments.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:08.430
And thanks for watching.

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:11.780
[MUSIC PLAYING]

